.TH KERO 1 "2026-11-17" "Kero 2.1.35" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kero \- terminal sessions that keep running, for you and your agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kero
.br
.B kero
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kero is a terminal app whose sessions live in a background process (\fBkerod\fR) and keep
running when the window closes. Run without arguments, \fBkero\fR opens the app. The commands
below start, drive and read sessions and panes from a shell, so that scripts and coding agents
can use them. A \fITARGET\fR is a session or pane id; by default it is the pane the command runs
in (\fI$KERO_PANE\fR). The full text for every command is printed by \fBkero \-\-help\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ls " [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-a\fR]"
List sessions and their panes.
.TP
.BR new " [\fB\-p\fR \fIPROJECT\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-d\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-w\fR] [\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-worktree\fR \fIBRANCH\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fICMD\fR...]"
Start a session and print its id.
.TP
.BR split " [\fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-\-right\fR|\fB\-\-down\fR|\fB\-\-left\fR|\fB\-\-up\fR] [\fB\-r\fR \fIRATIO\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fICMD\fR...]"
Start a pane beside a pane and print its id.
.TP
.BR send " \fITARGET\fR \fITEXT\fR...,  " key " \fITARGET\fR \fIKEY\fR..."
Type text into a pane, or press keys.
.TP
.BR prompt " \fITARGET\fR \fITEXT\fR..."
Send text and Enter, wait until the pane stops working, then print its screen.
.TP
.BR read " [\fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fILINES\fR]"
Print a pane's screen.
.TP
.BR wait " [\fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-\-for\fR \fISTATUSES\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDUR\fR]"
Wait until a pane stops working or reaches a status.
.TP
.BR events ", " status ", " diff
Watch events, print status, or show the changes in a pane's git worktree.
.TP
.B browser
Drive a browser pane (needs Remote Control, in Settings \(rg Agents).
.TP
.BR history ", " resume
List the conversations agents ran in panes, and resume one.
.TP
.BR rename ", " focus ", " close ", " restart ", " notify ", " report
Manage and report on sessions and panes.
.TP
.BR do ", " actions
Run an app action, as its menus do, and list them.
.TP
.BR config " {path|show|edit|check}"
Work with the configuration file.
.TP
.BR projects ", " hosts ", " clients ", " skill
Projects, other machines Kero reaches, connected clients, and teaching coding agents to use
\fBkero\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KERO_SESSION, KERO_PANE
Set inside every pane; the default target.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /Applications/Kero.app
The application; \fI/usr/local/bin/kero\fR is a symlink to its executable.
.SH SEE ALSO
Online documentation: \fIdocs/cli.md\fR in the source tree.
